**Design Notes:**
The module implements an 8-bit signed adder with overflow detection. The sum is computed using combinational addition, and overflow is detected when both operands have the same sign (MSB) but the result has a different sign. This is achieved by checking if the MSBs of the inputs are equal and the MSB of the sum differs.

[BEGIN]
module TopModule
(
  input  logic [7:0] a,
  input  logic [7:0] b,
  output logic [7:0] s,
  output logic overflow
);

  // Combinational sum and overflow detection
  assign s = a + b;
  assign overflow = (a[7] == b[7]) && (a[7] != s[7]);

